      "summary": "Network People Services Technologies Limited has informed the Exchange regarding 'Intimation of Contract to Build a Super App for a Leading Telecom Conglomerate's Operations in Sri Lanka pursuant to Regulation 30 read with Schedule III Part A Para C of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015.'.",
      "pdf_link": "https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/NPST_01102026154951_SE_Intimation_of_Sri_Lanka_order_01102026_signed.pdf",
      "pdf_extracted_text": "ISIN: INE0FFK01017 Date: 01.10.2026 To, The National Stock Exchange of India BSE Limited Limited, Exchange Plaza, NSE Corporate Relationship Department Building, Bandra Kurla Complex, Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Bandra East, Mumbai-400 0513 Fax: Dalal Street, Mumbai – 400 001 022-26598237, 022-26598238 Scrip Code: 544396 SYMBOL: NPST Subject: Intimation of Contract to Build a Super App for a Leading Telecom Conglomerate's Operations in Sri Lanka pursuant to Regulation 30 read with Schedule III Part A Para C of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015. Respected Sir/Madam, In compliance with Regulation 30, read with Schedule III, Part A, Para C of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, we are pleased to announce that Network People Services Technologies Limited (NPST) has secured a contract to build a Super App for the Sri Lankan operations of a leading telecom conglomerate with a presence across multiple countries. This engagement marks NPST's entry into the telecom-led digital ecosystem space in Sri Lanka and reflects the Company's growing capability to deliver large-scale, consumer-facing digital platforms beyond its banking and payments clientele, further strengthening its international presence. The project entrusts NPST with the design and development of a comprehensive Super App, integrating multiple digital services onto a single platform, built to be secure, scalable and compliant with applicable regulatory and industry standards for the Sri Lankan market. This engagement reinforces NPST's reputation as a trusted technology partner capable of building large-scale consumer digital ecosystems for global conglomerates. Given the telecom client's multi-country footprint, NPST views this as an opportunity to demonstrate its platform capabilities for potential clients in other markets, further catalysing the Company's international growth strategy. Kindly acknowledge and take the same on records. Thanking You, Yours Faithfully, For Network People Services Technologies Limited Chetna Chawla Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Membership No: A64291"
